# JSX Spread-Object Prop Pattern

When a JSX element has more than 2 props, ALWAYS use the spread-object pattern instead of individual prop attributes.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — 3+ props → spread-object
<Image {...{
  src: '/images/heart.svg',
  alt: '',
  width: 12,
  height: 10,
  unoptimized: true,
}} />

// ❌ BAD — individual attributes when 3+ props
<Image
  src="/images/heart.svg"
  alt=""
  width={12}
  height={10}
  unoptimized
/>
```

- 2 props or fewer: individual attributes are fine
- 3 or more props: MUST use `{...{ key: value }}` spread-object syntax
- Boolean props must be explicit: `unoptimized: true`, not shorthand `unoptimized`
